WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.600
Fill a glass from the tap.

2
00:00:01.650 --> 00:00:05.050
It's clear, it's safe,
and you can drink it.

3
00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:07.230
But it didn't start out that way.

4
00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:11.170
It may have begun in a river
or a reservoir, carrying mud,

5
00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:14.950
dissolved substances and microbes
that could make you ill.

6
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:18.810
So what has to happen to that
water before it reaches your tap?

7
00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:21.930
And when it arrives,
is it actually pure?

8
00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:25.390
In this mission, you'll find
out what a chemist means by pure

9
00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:26.050
water.

10
00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:29.110
You'll see how filtering
removes solids,

11
00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:32.610
and how chlorine and other
treatments kill microbes.

12
00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:37.050
Your mission: explain how river
water becomes safe to drink.
